# Call lifecycle

Sources: `packages/web/src/shared/lib/call-state.ts`, `packages/web/src/features/jitsi-call/jitsi-call-modal-shell.hook.ts`, and Electron call IPC in `packages/electron/src/main.ts`.

- Use the existing `callState` lifecycle for native awareness, wake locks, title/media-session state, and participant changes.
- Start/end at the lifecycle boundaries used by the call owner. Merely opening a settings or prejoin view must not create an independent active call.
- End and release resources on leave, failure, unmount, and runtime disposal. Cleanup must tolerate repeated calls.
- Do not introduce a second power-save blocker or competing media-session/title owner.
- Preserve minimized-call behavior: hiding the modal is not necessarily leaving the call.
